  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes differences in probabilities of favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of such an outcome. In this case, the reason would favor Lottery A (50% chance of 0 Euros vs. 0% in B). The individual does mention a 50% chance, but not in the context of favoring a better probabilistic outcome — rather, it is used to justify focusing on the worst-case scenario. The individual’s justification is based on minimizing the maximum possible loss (a minimax or risk-averse strategy), not on maximizing the probability of a favorable result. There is no evidence that the individual compared the probabilities of favorable outcomes between the lotteries or used such a comparison in their decision. The consideration of probability is minimal and serves a different reasoning purpose. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
